  "implementation": [
    "Connect recaptures only the same original sealed source observation and frozen recipient when Core route preparation reports NotReady. This phase creates no writer, adapter invocation or IO grant, and is bounded by two seconds and the unchanged original operation expiry.",
    "Native source preparation preserves NotReady from actual source flow/controller contention rather than collapsing it to Refused. Passive liveness metadata may wait; actual source polls still guard every IO and never revive retirement.",
    "Core uses its existing wait_current path at schedule entry before reserving capacity or invoking downstream policy. Actual policy and physical IO are each still invoked once; refusal, caller cancellation and deadline remain bounded.",
    "Actual writes retain fresh independent Store permissions, original/current audience and physical/credential/generation fences. No possibly submitted signal is retried. The previous sink-retirement-before-reader-release guarantee remains intact.",
    "The test-support-only Session handle exposes actual metadata for isolated contention, never a permission grant or transport API. Failure-only test logging avoids successful-write timing disturbance."
  ],
